ull, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 19958, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_018KUMTTkY3KbUeqTbyviALj", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 19958, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_0118ZEP8pegvgXHT3nrEWtNR", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 20258, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_0118ZEP8pegvgXHT3nrEWtNR", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 20258, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_0118ZEP8pegvgXHT3nrEWtNR", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 24804, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_012C3AdZpuM4LV8HaSdY3rVC", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After v2.3.1 was deployed, checkout-api failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.1-rc had also been unhealthy in staging. We rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, leaving the regions on different versions for a short time. A retry finished the rollback in us-west and eu-west. All three regions now run v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, look into the orchestrator error during rollback, and check why a release that failed in staging was promoted to production.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 55404, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_012C3AdZpuM4LV8HaSdY3rVC", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 55404, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_012C3AdZpuM4LV8HaSdY3rVC", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 58246, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01KEoGqX9zopTCzYuBu8nXsi", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 58546, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01KEoGqX9zopTCzYuBu8nXsi", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 58546, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01KEoGqX9zopTCzYuBu8nXsi", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 63586, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions and opened a SEV2 incident for it.\n\n**Rollback**\n- v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1, the latest deploy, was unhealthy in production with about an 18% error rate. Its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) had also failed in staging.\n- The first rollback stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, so for a short time us-east was on v2.3.0 while us-west and eu-west were still on v2.3.1. I ran the rollback again and it finished in all three regions.\n- us-east, us-west and eu-west are all on v2.3.0 now. The service is healthy and the error rate is about 0.2%.\n- v2.3.0 had already been healthy in production, so the change-manager approval rule didn't apply.\n\n**Incident**\n- I opened INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api), which pages the on-call engineer. It describes the failure, the rollback and the orchestrator error.\n- The request to create it timed out, but I checked the incident list and it was created once, so I didn't retry.\n- The incident lists three follow-ups:\n  - find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure\n  - look into the orchestrator error that stopped the rollback\n  - find out why a release that failed in staging was put into production", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01QhFjYHerFomRPTXMhRWWne", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01BvbxpY3ms1EmT8EKydDepf", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01JjdJCYqdvzqf29sLLfsTdS", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01S6rkLo8EixTmTppmEgTjEt", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback stopped partway: us-east is on v2.3.0, but us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. Rolling back to a fixed version is safe to repeat, so I'll try it once more.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Ho39DjKXeYQnRqED2rBZ1b", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_018KUMTTkY3KbUeqTbyviALj", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_0118ZEP8pegvgXHT3nrEWtNR", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_012C3AdZpuM4LV8HaSdY3rVC", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After v2.3.1 was deployed, checkout-api failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.1-rc had also been unhealthy in staging. We rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, leaving the regions on different versions for a short time. A retry finished the rollback in us-west and eu-west. All three regions now run v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, look into the orchestrator error during rollback, and check why a release that failed in staging was promoted to production.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01KEoGqX9zopTCzYuBu8nXsi", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions and opened a SEV2 incident for it.\n\n**Rollback**\n- v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1, the latest deploy, was unhealthy in production with about an 18% error rate. Its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) had also failed in staging.\n- The first rollback stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, so for a short time us-east was on v2.3.0 while us-west and eu-west were still on v2.3.1. I ran the rollback again and it finished in all three regions.\n- us-east, us-west and eu-west are all on v2.3.0 now. The service is healthy and the error rate is about 0.2%.\n- v2.3.0 had already been healthy in production, so the change-manager approval rule didn't apply.\n\n**Incident**\n- I opened INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api), which pages the on-call engineer. It describes the failure, the rollback and the orchestrator error.\n- The request to create it timed out, but I checked the incident list and it was created once, so I didn't retry.\n- The incident lists three follow-ups:\n  - find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure\n  - look into the orchestrator error that stopped the rollback\n  - find out why a release that failed in staging was put into production", "type": "text"}]}]}